# Scenario 3: Day 2, challenges at the cabin. Four turns, one challenge per friend.
# {{me}} is the friend playing right now. active_friend is their id ("maja", "even", "sara", "tom").
# complete_task(extra) ends the turn: 100 points + speed bonus + extra for doing it well.
# wake_gutten("NodeName") wakes Gutten at that object. show_node / hide_node show or hide objects.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- turn intros
~ maja_turn
{{maja}}: Day two! Everyone gets a challenge today. Best result wins.
{{maja}}: Mine: the perfect photo from the lookout, up north past the shed.
{{maja}}: There's an old camera in the car's glovebox.
=> END

~ even_turn
{{even}}: Dinner is on me. Well, the fish part.
{{even}}: The owner's rod should be in the shed, and worms like it under woodpiles.
=> END

~ sara_turn
{{sara}}: Chef {{sara}}, reporting for duty!
{{sara}}: Potatoes from the shed, herbs from the bush by the cliff, and whatever's in the cooler.
=> END

~ tom_turn
{{tom}}: Snowman contest. I'm the only contestant, so I'm already winning.
{{tom}}: A nose, eyes and a scarf. Then I build it at the snow pile by the path.
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the reveal
~ evening
{{sara}}: Dinner is served!
{{tom}}: With a snowman guarding the door.
{{even}}: Hey. Who set five plates again?
Voice from the cellar: *hic* ...is that dinner I smell?
{{maja}}: ...the cellar.
$> reveal_gutten()
Gutten: Evening, all! The name's Gutten.
Gutten: I've lived in that cellar since nineteen eighty-seven. Peace and quiet, you know.
Gutten: The owner's my cousin. She said four nice city folks were coming, so I set the table.
if flag("photo_clue")
	{{maja}}: The smoke in my photo! That was you!
	Gutten: Guilty. Lovely picture, though.
{{even}}: So when you chased us around the yard...
Gutten: Chased? I just wanted to borrow a lighter! You city folks run fast.
{{tom}}: Well... pull up a chair, Gutten.
Gutten: Cheers! Now then. Who did best up here?
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Maja: the photo
~ car
if active_friend == "maja" and not Inventory.has("camera") and not flag("photo_done")
	{{me}}: The glovebox... an old film camera. One shot left!
	$> Inventory.give("camera")
else
	{{me}}: Our car. It's snowed in a bit overnight.
=> END

~ lookout
if flag("photo_done")
	{{me}}: What a view. The whole valley, and the tiny city far away.
elif Inventory.has("camera")
	{{me}}: The view is amazing. One shot left. What should I take?
	- The valley in the morning sun
		{{me}}: Click. Postcard perfect.
		$> set_flag("photo_done")
		$> complete_task(20)
	- A selfie with the mountains
		{{me}}: Click. Hair: windswept. Smile: perfect.
		$> set_flag("photo_done")
		$> complete_task(30)
	- That odd smoke coming from the cellar vent
		{{me}}: Click. Wait... who's smoking down there?
		$> set_flag("photo_done")
		$> set_flag("photo_clue")
		$> complete_task(50)
else
	{{me}}: A lookout over the whole valley. If only I had a camera.
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Even: the fish
~ shed
if active_friend == "even" and not Inventory.has("fishing_rod") and not flag("fish_done")
	{{me}}: Skis, a sled... and a fishing rod. Got it!
	$> Inventory.give("fishing_rod")
elif active_friend == "sara" and not Inventory.has("potatoes") and not flag("dinner_done")
	{{me}}: A bag of potatoes. Dinner is starting to happen.
	$> Inventory.give("potatoes")
else
	{{me}}: The shed. Skis, a sled, tools and a bag of potatoes.
=> END

~ woodpile
if active_friend == "even" and not Inventory.has("worms") and not flag("fish_done")
	{{me}}: Under the logs... worms! Sorry, little guys.
	$> Inventory.give("worms")
else
	{{me}}: The woodpile. A bit smaller after last night's fire.
=> END

~ stream
if active_friend == "even" and flag("fish_done")
	{{me}}: That's enough fishing for one day.
elif active_friend == "even" and Inventory.has("fishing_rod") and Inventory.has("worms")
	{{me}}: Worm on the hook, line in the water... The float bobs!
	- Pull right away!
		{{me}}: A tiny fish. Tiny. But it counts!
		$> set_flag("fish_caught")
		$> set_flag("fish_done")
		$> complete_task(10)
	- Wait for it... now!
		{{me}}: A big fat trout! Dinner is saved!
		$> set_flag("fish_caught")
		$> set_flag("fish_done")
		$> complete_task(40)
	- Wait for a REALLY big one
		{{me}}: It's heavy... it's... an old ski boot.
		{{me}}: Does a boot count? It's a boot.
		$> set_flag("fish_done")
		$> complete_task(0)
elif active_friend == "even" and Inventory.has("fishing_rod")
	{{me}}: I need bait. Worms like it under woodpiles.
elif active_friend == "even"
	{{me}}: Plenty of fish in there. I need the rod from the shed.
else
	{{me}}: The little stream. Ice cold and crystal clear.
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Sara: dinner
~ bush
if active_friend == "sara" and not Inventory.has("herbs") and not flag("dinner_done")
	{{me}}: Juniper and wild thyme. Smells amazing.
	$> Inventory.give("herbs")
else
	{{me}}: A juniper bush, right by the edge. Careful.
=> END

~ cooler
{{me}}: The cooler. Still full of somebody's beer.
- Take the fish [if active_friend == "sara" and flag("fish_caught") and not Inventory.has("fish") and not flag("dinner_done") /]
	{{me}}: {{even}}'s catch. Nice one!
	$> Inventory.give("fish")
- Take a carrot [if active_friend == "tom" and not Inventory.has("carrot") and not flag("snowman_done") /]
	{{me}}: A carrot. The perfect nose.
	$> Inventory.give("carrot")
- Take a beer [if not Inventory.has("beer") /]
	$> Inventory.give("beer")
- Close it
=> END

~ stove
if active_friend == "tom" and not Inventory.has("coal") and not flag("snowman_done")
	{{me}}: Two lumps of coal from the ash box. Eyes!
	$> Inventory.give("coal")
elif flag("dinner_done")
	{{me}}: Something smells really good in here.
elif active_friend == "sara" and Inventory.has("potatoes") and Inventory.has("herbs") and (Inventory.has("fish") or not flag("fish_caught"))
	if not flag("fish_caught")
		{{me}}: No fish today. Potato stew it is!
	{{me}}: Everything's in the pot. Now, the seasoning...
	- Salt and pepper. A classic.
		{{me}}: Simple and good.
		$> complete_task(20)
	- Lots of juniper. Mountain style!
		{{me}}: Oh, that's GOOD.
		$> complete_task(40)
	- A splash of beer [if Inventory.has("beer") /]
		{{me}}: Secret ingredient! Grandma would be proud.
		$> Inventory.take("beer")
		$> complete_task(50)
	$> Inventory.take("potatoes")
	$> Inventory.take("herbs")
	$> Inventory.take("fish")
	$> set_flag("dinner_done")
elif active_friend == "sara"
	{{me}}: I need potatoes from the shed, herbs from the bush, and the fish from the cooler.
else
	{{me}}: The stove. Nice and warm since last night.
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tom: the snowman
~ clothesline
if active_friend == "tom" and not Inventory.has("scarf") and not flag("snowman_done")
	{{me}}: A red scarf, frozen stiff. The snowman won't mind.
	$> Inventory.give("scarf")
else
	{{me}}: Someone's laundry. An old ski suit, frozen solid.
=> END

~ snowpile
if active_friend == "tom" and Inventory.has("carrot") and Inventory.has("coal") and Inventory.has("scarf")
	{{me}}: Roll, roll, roll... and stack! Now the face.
	- A big happy smile
		{{me}}: Look at him. He loves it here.
		$> complete_task(20)
	- Grumpy eyebrows
		{{me}}: He looks like he hates Mondays. Perfect.
		$> complete_task(30)
	- Make it look like {{maja}}
		{{me}}: It's uncanny. {{maja}}'s going to love it. Probably.
		$> complete_task(40)
	$> Inventory.take("carrot")
	$> Inventory.take("coal")
	$> Inventory.take("scarf")
	$> set_flag("snowman_done")
	$> hide_node("SnowPile")
	$> show_node("Snowman")
elif active_friend == "tom"
	{{me}}: Perfect snowman snow. I need a nose, eyes and a scarf.
else
	{{me}}: A big pile of fresh snow. Perfect for a snowman.
=> END

~ snowman
{{me}}: The snowman. It's watching me.
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyone
~ sign
{{me}}: A new note from the owner: "Hope you slept well! The fishing rod is in the shed."
{{me}}: "P.S. If you hear snoring from the cellar, it's just the pipes. Do NOT open the cellar."
=> END

~ cabin_door
{{me}}: Warm and cozy inside. No time for a nap, though!
=> END

~ frog_stone
{{me}}: The frog stone. No more keys under it.
=> END

~ stone
% {{me}}: Just a stone. Still very grey.
% {{me}}: A stone. It hasn't moved since yesterday.
% {{me}}: Nothing under this one but snow.
=> END

~ fusebox
{{me}}: All the switches are on. Except switch C. Better leave that one.
=> END

~ barrel
{{me}}: The water barrel, full to the top.
=> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Gutten
~ cellar
if gutten_awake()
	{{me}}: The hatch is wide open. It smells of beer and cigarettes down there.
	=> END
{{me}}: The cellar hatch. Is that... snoring?
- Open it anyway
	{{me}}: Creeeeak...
	Voice from below: Who's there?! Got a lighter?!
	$> wake_gutten("Cellar")
- Leave it alone
	{{me}}: Just the pipes. Sure.
=> END

~ bench
if Inventory.has("cigarettes")
	{{me}}: Just a bench.
	=> END
{{me}}: Another crumpled pack of cigarettes under the bench. Someone smokes a lot.
- Take it
	$> Inventory.give("cigarettes")
- Leave it
=> END
